# Modeling: The Right Tool for the Job.

**Authors:** Gavanasen, Varut, Hussain, S. Tariq

## Abstract
Reviews the different types of models that can be used in groundwater modeling. Discusses the flow and contaminant transport models in the saturated zone, flow and contaminant transport in variably saturated flow regime, vapor transport, biotransformation models, multiphase models, optimization algorithms, and potentials pitfalls of using these models. (Contains 12 references.) (MDH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ476627

